tion":"1785455034121986073-4fdb15f5-2312-4b43-a4b5-acbda1f8e34a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d3baab99a6292aa7158d29c030414cc1a6fdd4cf386a3481294ea02e002be599","event_uuid":"8f1f053f-f0dd-45fd-8396-3ba3800ce04b","position":{"commit_sha":"1afbdd7c1b1f0812c7148aa7b483c04114fb05d5","position":"1785455715089883001-8f1f053f-f0dd-45fd-8396-3ba3800ce04b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"68b3c7255bcc85351694fb3a2ce90fe8b7f4125f694c2d460fd28dd9f13c367e","event_uuid":"9e140141-6eea-468b-aa0d-3f5f911ce5f4","position":{"commit_sha":"103bc36f4e5afa1606d00ea2f4b924881dd0396c","position":"1785455757091046001-9e140141-6eea-468b-aa0d-3f5f911ce5f4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"cbefdd3f533afa373a43995497f7aa2552c96bcd05a6afab47758aa202b06783","event_uuid":"6a990d34-831f-4461-abc3-8a1707891488","position":{"commit_sha":"838f6cc665879bf2b589044ae34fb3014ece7141","position":"1785455758774782001-6a990d34-831f-4461-abc3-8a1707891488"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-220_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"b707f729-f629-4867-9965-f2ea0e303433","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"LANDED as change 1070, merged to main (commit b91cda9b3).\n\nThe fixture now asserts BOTH halves of the virginity invariant:\n  conftest.py:86   assert rebar.list_tickets() == []   (inside the MonkeyPatch context)\n  conftest.py:103  assert not (repo / '.rebar').exists()\n\nPlacement was forced, not stylistic: the tickets check needs REBAR_ROOT and cwd pinned at the template, and the post-build assertions at :103 run AFTER the MonkeyPatch context exits. That is why the .rebar check can be a plain filesystem test at :103 and this one cannot.\n\nProven load-bearing before push, per the Testing section: seeding a ticket into the template build made the fixture raise 'template must be built with no tickets'; removing the seed returned tests/interfaces to 1397 passed / 12 skipped — identical to before the change, satisfying the 'same collected/passed counts' criterion. make lint and make typecheck clean.\n\nWhy this was worth its own change rather than an evidence comment on 699f: a test-level check only protects runs that SELECT that test, so a narrowed 'pytest tests/interfaces/store' had no protection at all. Asserting at construction fires once per worker before any test runs and covers every consumer.","timestamp":1785455715089883001}],"created_at":1785454159589506001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"5eff40ac-c716-482c-9971-8e81073ca553","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"699f-fc7e-2598-4636"},{"link_uuid":"8b7c059f-6682-436a-a687-36970028289f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"76d5-31f9-9952-4f09"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nTicket 699f replaced the per-test store build in `tests/interfaces/conftest.py` with a per-worker template that each test copies. Its acceptance criterion read: \"The template fixture asserts it is virgin (no tickets, no `<repo>/.rebar/`).\"\n\nThe landed change (Gerrit 1063, merged) satisfies only HALF of that. `_rebar_repo_template` asserts `not (repo / \".rebar\").exists()` but never asserts the template carries no tickets. The no-tickets half is checked only by a separate test, `tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py::test_template_stays_virgin`. The completion verifier caught this and correctly refused to close 699f.\n\nWhy this matters rather than being a wording nit: the invariant is that the template must NEVER be pre-seeded. Several tests in the tier assert on emptiness (session-log counts in `tests/interfaces/queries/test_recent_session_logs.py` and `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_session_log_capture.py`) and hold only because nothing seeds the template. The obvious next optimisation -- pre-warming the template with tickets so tests skip setup -- would silently invert those assertions.\n\nA fixture-level assertion fails at CONSTRUCTION, once per worker, before any test runs, and covers every consumer. A test-level assertion fires only when that one test is selected, so a narrowed run such as `pytest tests/interfaces/store` has no protection at all. Closing that gap is the reason to fix this properly rather than argue the criterion into compliance.\n\n## Approach\nAdd the missing assertion to `_rebar_repo_template` in `tests/interfaces/conftest.py`, immediately after `rebar.init_repo()` and the root commit, INSIDE the existing `pytest.MonkeyPatch.context()` block. It must sit inside that block because the assertion needs `REBAR_ROOT` and cwd pinned at the template; the context exits before the current post-build assertions run, which is why the existing `.rebar` check is a plain filesystem test.\n\nKeep the existing `.rebar` assertion where it is: it needs no environment and reads more clearly beside the other post-build checks.\n\nRejected alternative: leave the check in `test_template_stays_virgin` only and record evidence on 699f to satisfy the verifier. The criterion would then read as met while the narrowed-run gap above stays open. That is gaming the gate, not meeting it.\n\nRejected alternative: assert at the filesystem level (no ticket directories under `.tickets-tracker`) to avoid needing the pinned environment. That works, but it duplicates knowledge of the store layout that `rebar.list_tickets()` already owns, and would miss a ticket recorded anywhere the layout check does not look.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/interfaces/conftest.py` -- one assertion inside the template fixture's MonkeyPatch context.\n\n`test_template_stays_virgin` STAYS. It is not made redundant: it also asserts `.rebar` absence from a test context and documents the invariant where a reader of the sentinel file will look for it. This ticket adds enforcement at construction; it does not move the existing check.\n\n## Testing\nNo new behavior -- this adds an assertion to existing test infrastructure, so no new test is warranted.\n\nThe assertion must be shown to be load-bearing rather than decorative: seed a ticket into the template right after the build, confirm the fixture raises, then remove the seed and confirm the tier passes. That is a temporary local check; the durable evidence is the tier passing with the assertion in place.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `_rebar_repo_template` in `tests/interfaces/conftest.py` asserts the freshly built template has no tickets, inside the MonkeyPatch context where REBAR_ROOT and cwd are pinned.\n- [ ] The existing `.rebar` absence assertion is retained.\n- [ ] `tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py::test_template_stays_virgin` is retained and passes.\n- [ ] `python -m pytest tests/interfaces -q` passes with the same collected/passed counts as before this change.\n- [ ] `make lint` passes.\n- [ ] `make typecheck` passes.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/interfaces/conftest.py","reason":"assert no tickets inside the template fixture MonkeyPatch context"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","76d5-31f9-9952-4f09"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"9e140141-6eea-468b-aa0d-3f5f911ce5f4","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"446c-1d56-9163-499d","ticket_type":"task","title":"Assert template has no tickets inside the fixture, not only in a test","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["6d8a0e8c-744c-434b-9267-65398ba5a47a","83028afc-49f2-41c6-8358-73f0b620ffa2","5eff40ac-c716-482c-9971-8e81073ca553","0473468f-b6cc-417d-b886-b08418b8a22b","4b441f6c-967c-486c-ad0b-35ce4e1e92df","52876382-a378-4e1d-92cd-675779425028","4fdb15f5-2312-4b43-a4b5-acbda1f8e34a","8b7c059f-6682-436a-a687-36970028289f","8f1f053f-f0dd-45fd-8396-3ba3800ce04b","9e140141-6eea-468b-aa0d-3f5f911ce5f4","6a990d34-831f-4461-abc3-8a1707891488"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659562192691001,"uuid":"1c962445-8f7e-4ba3-9e7e-8d7205c19f0e"}